# Gauge-orbit prerequisites for the approved Singer obstruction

Run `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`. Root approved three additional mathematics A/B pairs, preserving all fifty-five existing pair identities. This scaffold is authoring direction, not proof acceptance. Integrate only through the root-owned drained native append route.

Full item statements, local proof contracts, item DAG, supplier byte pins and actual source reading limits: [gauge-slice-prerequisite-plan.json](gauge-slice-prerequisite-plan.json). Resolution and mathematical cautions: [gauge-slice-source-repair.md](gauge-slice-source-repair.md). Exact source evidence: [source-reading.json](gauge-slice-source-repair/source-reading.json).

All new items are draft `domain: mathematics`, `library: mathematics`, category `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`. Use AC explicitly through the imported analysis/topology suppliers and propagate it. A cited established theorem awaiting local proof is an authoring obligation, not an open-problem supplier. Write complete proof carriers and ordinary item contracts; never activate the proposed statements as if they were proved. Each A/B page has frontmatter only, and B examples remain leaves.

## Sobolev and Smooth Gauge-Orbit Geometry

A page: `qftx-sobolev-gauge-orbit-geometry`; B companion: `qftx-sobolev-gauge-orbit-geometry-examples`.

Required earlier pages (exact imported suppliers and current in-run geometry): `qftx-gauge-geometry`, `banach-space-differential-calculus-and-banach-manifolds`, `compact-laplace-type-operators-and-hodge-representatives`, `compact-operators-and-riesz-schauder-theory`, `gauge-groups-and-representation-theory-interfaces`, `relations-functions-and-quotients`, `sobolev-poincare-and-morrey-inequalities`, `unitary-representations-positive-type-and-gns`, `picard-lindelof-and-first-order-odes`.

A-page inventory:

- `def-qftx-smooth-sobolev-gauge-configuration` (definition): Smooth and Sobolev configuration and reduced gauge spaces.
- `lem-qftx-gauge-sobolev-calculus` (lemma): Sobolev gauge calculus and smooth gauge action.
- `lem-qftx-gauge-stabilizer-and-properness` (lemma): Gauge stabilizers and properness of the Sobolev action.
- `lem-qftx-covariant-laplacian-sobolev-splitting` (lemma): Rough-coefficient covariant Green inverse and Coulomb splitting.
- `thm-qftx-sobolev-smooth-irreducible-gauge-bundle` (theorem): Sobolev and smooth irreducible gauge-orbit principal bundles.

B-page worked examples: `ex-qftx-covariantly-constant-stabilizer`, `ex-qftx-coulomb-chart-linearization`.

Start with integer k > dim(M)/2 + 1, H^k connections, H^(k+1) gauge transformations, a smooth reference connection and a finite bundle atlas. Define smooth section topology and quotient topology explicitly. Prove properness as well as the near-identity IFT chart: the latter alone cannot exclude a far gauge transformation returning to a small slice. Imported elliptic Green theory has smooth coefficients; author its needed rough-coefficient extension. Prove regularity compatibility to obtain the C-infinity bundle. Mitter–Viallet Theorems5.28–5.29 and Narasimhan–Ramadas §§2–4 guide the reconstruction but do not waive their referenced auxiliary steps.

## Topology of Irreducible Connection Spaces

A page: `qftx-irreducible-connection-topology`; B companion: `qftx-irreducible-connection-topology-examples`.

Required earlier pages (exact imported suppliers and current in-run geometry): `qftx-sobolev-gauge-orbit-geometry`, `compactness`, `higher-homotopy-groups-and-cofiber-sequences`, `sard-theorem-and-transversality`, `whitney-embedding-tubular-neighbourhoods-and-approximation`, `euclidean-ordinary-differential-equations-with-smooth-dependence`.

A-page inventory:

- `lem-qftx-irreducible-finite-holonomy-witness` (lemma): Finite holonomy witnesses for irreducibility.
- `lem-qftx-relative-finite-parameter-irreducible-avoidance` (lemma): Relative finite-parameter avoidance of reducible connections.
- `thm-qftx-irreducible-connections-weak-contractibility` (theorem): Weak contractibility of the irreducible connection locus.

B-page worked examples: `ex-qftx-relative-affine-disk-filling`.

Use representation irreducibility, not the stronger full-holonomy condition for general N. The JSON supplies the constructive finite-loop proof route: finite boundary holonomy witnesses; disjoint independent loop-control arcs; transported bump perturbations; relative smoothing/collar; incidence manifold over Gr_C(k,N) with dimension deficit2(r−1)k(N−k); finite-dimensional Sard to choose good parameters. Prove each construction and uniform estimate. Fill sphere families first in affine all-connections, then repair relative boundary to prove weak contractibility. Singer Theorem2 supplies an outline; do not cite its infinite-codimension slogan as a complete proof.

## Sphere Gauge Groups and Section Obstructions

A page: `qftx-gauge-group-sphere-homotopy`; B companion: `qftx-gauge-group-sphere-homotopy-examples`.

Required earlier pages (exact imported suppliers and current in-run geometry): `qftx-sobolev-gauge-orbit-geometry`, `fibrations-fiber-bundles-and-homotopy-exact-sequences`, `higher-homotopy-groups-and-cofiber-sequences`, `hurewicz-whitehead-freudenthal-and-cw-approximation`, `whitney-embedding-tubular-neighbourhoods-and-approximation`.

A-page inventory:

