For each N ≥ 2 and every fixed smooth principal SU(N) bundle P over S4, also S3, give the affine space A of smooth connections and its gauge group G their C-infinity section topologies and A/G the quotient topology. There is no continuous right inverse of A → A/G. In fact the projection from the irreducible locus A* to A*/(G/Z_N) has no section. Irreducibility here means irreducibility of the holonomy representation on C^N; it must not be silently replaced by full SU(N) holonomy for N > 2. Singer announces a compact connected semisimple generalization, but writes the proof for SU(N). If a broader group class was approved independently, its central-cover/simple-factor reduction is an additional explicit proof obligation; it is not discharged by the abstract.

